      "type": "mcq",
      "difficulty": 1,
      "prompt": "Which part of a plant takes in water from the soil?",
      "options": [
        {
          "text": "the leaves",
          "why": "Leaves are up in the air. Their job is to make food using light."
        },
        {
          "text": "the flower",
          "why": "The flower's job is to make seeds."
        },
        {
          "text": "the roots"
        },
        {
          "text": "the stem",
          "why": "The stem carries water up the plant, but it does not take it from the soil."
        }
      ],
      "answer": 2,
      "hints": [
        "Think about which part touches the soil.",
        "Water is in the soil, under the ground.",
        "Picture a plant pulled out of a pot. Which part was in the soil?"
      ],
      "explanation": "The roots grow in the soil. They take in water and minerals and hold the plant in place."
    },
